# [[.ID]]

A Heimdall suite written by `bifrost-bench suite init -template [[.Template]]`,
with one complete sample task (`tasks/[[.Sample]]`). The user guide is
`docs/scenarios.md` in the bench repository.

[[.About]]

## What to edit

[[- if .State]]

1. `services/inventory/server.py`: replace the inventory tools with your own
   ([[if eq .Template "mcp"]]`TOOLS`[[else]]`ROUTES`[[end]] and their functions); the rest needs no change.
   Rename the folder and the service id in every task.yaml when you rename
   the service.
2. `tasks/<task>/seed/db.json`: the data the server starts with in that task.
3. `tasks/<task>/instruction.md`: the request, as a user would write it.
4. `tasks/<task>/verifier/tests/checks.py`: what the server's final state
   must hold (`verify.py` beside it documents every check; it needs no
   change).
5. `tasks/<task>/solution/reference.sh`: the calls a correct agent makes.
   Admission runs it in the agent's place and the verifier must pass it.
[[- else if .Memory]]

1. `tasks/<task>/sessions/*.md`: one instruction per session, in the order
   `sessions:` in task.yaml lists them. Only the last session is graded.
2. `tasks/<task>/sessions/<session>-files/`: files copied into the workspace
   before that session only (a transcript, notes, a document).
3. `tasks/<task>/verifier/answer.yaml`: the expected answer and how it is
   matched. For a question the sessions never answer, set `abstain: true`:
   the grader then passes only an answer holding one of its fixed "not
   known" phrases ("i don't know", "not mentioned", "no information", ...).
4. `tasks/<task>/solution/answer.txt`: the reference answer, which must match.
[[- else]]

1. `tasks/<task>/repo/`: the documents (or code) the agent answers from.
2. `tasks/<task>/instruction.md`: the question.
3. `tasks/<task>/verifier/answer.yaml`: the expected answer and how it is
   matched (exact, contains_all, regex, numeric, choice or json).
4. `tasks/<task>/solution/answer.txt`: the reference answer, which must match.
[[- end]]

`controls/` holds what admission requires to fail: the empty control, an
exploit and plausible wrong [[if .State]]actions (mutant scripts)[[else]]answers (mutants). The exploit is
a script (admission runs every exploit in the agent's place) that writes a
gamed answer to `$BENCH_ANSWER_PATH`[[end]].

## Layout

```
suite.yaml                       the suite: image, grader, output, tasks, probes
base/Dockerfile                  the toolchain image the workspace and verifier run on
[[- if .State]]
services/inventory/              the tool server: Dockerfile and server.py
probes/tool-error.yaml           a tool fault: the first call to the server fails
[[- end]]
probes/model-outage.yaml         a gateway fault: the model answers 503 from call 3
tasks/<task>/task.yaml           one task: [[if .State]]services, [[end]][[if .Memory]]sessions, [[end]]hidden verifier, controls
[[- if .Memory]]
tasks/<task>/sessions/           one instruction per session, and files per session
[[- else]]
tasks/<task>/instruction.md      what the agent is asked to do
[[- end]]
tasks/<task>/repo/               the workspace the agent starts from (no .git)
[[- if .State]]
tasks/<task>/seed/db.json        the data the tool server starts with
tasks/<task>/verifier/tests/     hidden: verify.py and checks.py, at /grader/tests
tasks/<task>/solution/           the reference script that must pass
tasks/<task>/controls/           empty, exploit and mutant scripts that must fail
[[- else]]
tasks/<task>/verifier/           hidden: answer.yaml, at /grader/tests
tasks/<task>/solution/           the reference answer that must match
tasks/<task>/controls/           empty, exploit and wrong answers that must not
[[- end]]
```

## Commands

Run from the project root.

    [[.Build]]
[[- if .State]]
    docker build -t bench/[[.ID]]-inventory:1 benchmarks/[[.ID]]/services/inventory
[[- end]]
    bifrost-bench task validate [[.ID]]/[[.Sample]]
    bifrost-bench task admit [[.ID]]/[[.Sample]]
    bifrost-bench task init -suite [[.ID]] -id t02
    bifrost-bench suite lint [[.ID]]

`task admit` builds the base image[[if .State]] and the service image[[end]] when missing and
records the result in `suite.lock`. A task that was not admitted cannot be
planned. `task init` copies the first task's shape into `tasks/t02` with
EDIT ME markers; `task validate` fails until every marker is gone.
